# API Changelog v1 vs. v1


## API Changes

### PUT /owners/{ownerId}/pets
- :warning: api removed without deprecation


### POST /pets/{petId}
- :warning: the request property `items/Ünïcode/price` became required
- :warning: removed the request property `items/Ünïcode/price/%20`
- :warning: removed the request property `items/Ünïcode/price/&anchor`
-  the request optional property `items/Ünïcode/price` became write-only
-  removed the deprecated request property `items/Ünïcode/price/id`
-  the `items/Ünïcode/price` request property `type` changed from `object` to `string` (backward compatible)
-  the response optional property `no/items/price` became write-only for the status `204` (media type: application/xml)
-  the response optional property `price` became write-only for the status `204` (media type: application/json; charset=utf-8)
-  the response property `no/items/price` became required for the status `204` (media type: application/xml)
-  the `no/items/price` response's property `type` changed from `object` to `string` for status `204` (media type: application/xml)
-  the `price` response's property `type` changed from `object` to `string` for status `204` (media type: application/json; charset=utf-8)
-  removed the deprecated required property `no/items/price/id` from the response with the `204` status (media type: application/xml)
-  removed the deprecated required property `price/id` from the response with the `204` status (media type: application/json; charset=utf-8)
-  removed the required write-only property `no/items/price/%20` from the response with the `204` status (media type: application/xml)
-  removed the required write-only property `no/items/price/&anchor` from the response with the `204` status (media type: application/xml)
-  removed the required write-only property `price/%20` from the response with the `204` status (media type: application/json; charset=utf-8)
-  removed the required write-only property `price/&anchor` from the response with the `204` status (media type: application/json; charset=utf-8)
-  the response write-only property `price` became required for the status `204` (media type: application/json; charset=utf-8)






